# Post-live-test automation improvements
Workstream-ID: lea-01
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/2
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: TODO.md, 2026-07-20 original improvement batch
Status: IN_REVIEW
Milestone: Reliable form interactions and graceful run shutdown
Dependencies: None

## Purpose
Reduce repeated manual interaction while retaining explicit, auditable form behavior.
This projection omits original user quotations and applicant-specific values.

## Tasks
- [x] Handle Ctrl+C with modal cleanup, aborted-attempt persistence and a summary.
- [x] Clean unreferenced screenshots without deleting retained application evidence.
- [x] Reuse an existing matching resume before attempting programmatic upload.
- [x] Log aligned score-pass and score-fail decisions.
- [x] Handle the configured phone-country code independently of the phone number.
- [x] Reuse learned answers from the database.
- [x] Accept terminal input or read a manually completed portal field back.
- [x] Leave already-correct prefilled controls unchanged.
- [ ] Qualify the original resume-upload and country-code cases against the live target.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Original implementation and focused regression tests are recorded.
- [x] Configuration and user-facing documentation are updated.
- [ ] Required live upload/country-code qualification is evidenced, with any selector tuning.

## Completion evidence
The original 2026-07-20 record attributes implementation to commit `a60b1f9`,
31 new regression cases and a 109-test green suite with Ruff/Black checks.
These are historical source claims, not checks rerun by this tracking migration.
The source explicitly leaves live qualification pending. Later resume-reuse
success does not independently prove the missing upload path. Publication and
human acceptance are separate; historical push statements are not current status.

## Completion log
- 2026-07-20: Original implementation and local verification recorded.
- 2026-11-06: Public-safe projection created; status intentionally remains
  IN_REVIEW rather than treating checked implementation tasks as completed live qualification.
  No new applications or browser interactions are authorized by this migration.
